# Everything C8 downloads or builds lands here and none of it is committed:
#   filament/            prebuilt arm64 release, tools/fetch_filament.sh (131 MB)
#   filament-src/        shallow clone of google/filament @ v1.75.0 (1.7 GB)
#   filament-build-x86_64/  its CMake build tree
#   filament-x86_64/     the collected x86_64 static libs
#   filament-universal/  the lipo'd arm64+x86_64 tree the universal app links
#   qt-universal/        official universal Qt via aqtinstall (1.3 GB)
#   .aqt-venv/           the venv aqtinstall lives in
# Pinned to Filament v1.75.0 per S3 REPORT.md §9 caveat 2; the SCRIPTS that
# produce all of the above are committed, so this is fully reproducible.
third_party/

# build trees
build/
build-*/

# C8 packaging outputs — the DMG/installer/AppImage/.deb are release artifacts,
# built by CI from the committed scripts, never committed themselves.
dist/
packaging/windows/staging/
packaging/windows/*.exe
packaging/linux/AppDir/
packaging/linux/deb/
packaging/linux/.tools/
packaging/linux/*.AppImage
packaging/linux/*.deb

# NOT ignored, on purpose: packaging/{macos/lidarscan.icns,macos/lidarscan.png,
# linux/lidarscan.png,windows/lidarscan.ico}. They are generated by
# tools/make_icon.sh, but they are committed because they are *build inputs*
# (NSIS needs the .ico at makensis time) and because make_icon.sh's high-quality
# resampling path needs macOS's `sips` — a Windows or Linux runner regenerating
# them would produce a worse icon than the one in the tree. Replace the artwork
# by editing make_icon.sh, re-running it, and committing the result.

# matc output
*.filamat

# Verification artefacts. The screenshots and the log ARE the C1 evidence and are
# tracked; the 394 KB synthetic byte stream and the .lscan it produces are
# regenerable in seconds by scripts/verify.sh and are not.
evidence/*-qtchrome.png
evidence/synth-d6.bin
evidence/synth.lscan/
